.TH smi-pki-create-self-signed-certificate "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-create-self-signed-certificate \- Self-sign a CSR with its own private key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-create-self-signed-certificate
.I PRIV_KEY_FILE CSR_FILE CERT_FILE DAYS EXT_FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Self-signs \fICSR_FILE\fR with \fIPRIV_KEY_FILE\fR into \fICERT_FILE\fR, valid \fIDAYS\fR days, applying \fIEXT_FILE\fR. Used for the Root CA.
It is a thin command line wrapper over the matching function in the file based PKI library
\fBpki.sh\fR, so each step of building a CA and signing certificates can be run and inspected
on its own. All material is passed as file names; the command fails if the underlying OpenSSL
operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-pki-ca-create (1),
.BR smi-pki-create-domain-cert (1),
.BR openssl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
